From f2049b099df9b4afd28b32ba2e840bd9a2edd9d7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 04:01:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat: wire curation into the UI, library shelves, 44px touch
 targets, mobile fixes

- cards, detail, search and filters now use content-data/apps.json (curated bilingual
  titles/summaries, audience, type); filters: Apps/Documents/Code x audience
- flagship apps lead the catalogue in curated order (src/content/apps.ts)
- library tabs are the curated shelves; folder matching is tolerant of case,
  underscores, trailing spaces and word-boundary prefixes (src/lib/shelf.ts)
- every interactive element >= 44px on all 7 pages (was 33-36px in header, 16-24px links)
- platform tiles: round dots, tidy captions, honest Cloudflare state
- card addresses show the informative part (/path on github.io); no duplicate platform
- phone home: name + portrait above the fold
- tests: shelf resolver, curation data integrity (32 total)
